&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll help eliminate quoting backlogs and drive high-volume, complex deal execution as Everlaw scales through a critical capacity surge. Acting as a strategic bridge between Sales, Customer Success, Finance, and Legal, you will manage end-to-end quoting and queue triage to ensure deal structures are scalable, reliable, and compliant while protecting long-term revenue integrity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a full-time, non-exempt position based in our Oakland, CA office with a hybrid work schedule: in office M/W/Th with the option to work from home on Tu/Fr.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end quoting for new business, renewals, and complex amendments using Salesforce CPQ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Salesforce and Zendesk queue, managing the intake, triage, and escalation of all Quote-to-Cash requests within defined SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Finance and Legal to navigate non-standard terms and resolve system inefficiencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in standardizing deal workflows and systemizing the escalation process within Salesforce to improve operational transparency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all deals adhere to established price books, discount thresholds, and Everlaw’s financial compliance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 5 years of experience in Deal Desk, Sales Operations, or Revenue Operations, including hands-on ownership of quoting for complex deal structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have advanced proficiency in Salesforce CPQ (or a similar tool), with deep experience configuring products, bundles, price rules, and troubleshooting quote logic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You balance short-term sales velocity with long-term revenue integrity, ensuring deals move quickly while adhering to pricing and compliance guardrails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a clear communicator who can articulate complex commercial concepts across Sales, Customer Success, Finance, Legal, and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are detail-oriented and experienced in managing high-volume queues in fast-paced SaaS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are authorized to work in the United States. Please note that at this time, Everlaw is not sponsoring U.S. employment visas for this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience or interest in exploring AI-driven tools or automation agents to streamline Deal Desk workflows and queue management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think you&#39;re missing some of the skills and are hesitant to apply? We do not believe in the &#39;perfect&#39; candidate and encourage you to apply if you feel you can bring value to our team. We often revisit candidates who may have applied for a different role if something comes up that&#39;s a better fit.&lt;/p&gt;
