&lt;p&gt;Everlaw is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Technical Program Manager, Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; to drive technical alignment, system ownership, and process enforcement across our Engineering team. In this high-visibility role, you will focus on Engineering Manager (EM) and Engineering Program Management (EPM) enablement, building self-service automation and tools that act as force multipliers across the entire organization. Ideally, you bring a background in software development within a program management function and a passion for turning complex technical requirements into elegant operational solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits within our Engineering department, where you will partner closely with senior engineering leadership to cultivate strategic relationships and unblock technical teams. You will bridge the gap between engineering infrastructure and business intelligence, helping to define and collect datasets that inform our data-driven decision-making. Your work will directly impact our engineering velocity, enabling multidisciplinary teams to execute with confidence, clarity, and autonomy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Getting started&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We want you to feel like part of the team early on! Our onboarding process will integrate you into the company with informative sessions on our product, policies, processes, and team structure and goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re excited for you to learn, grow, and contribute right away! We trust that you’ll bring experience and knowledge that will uplift and uplevel the team, but we don’t expect you to know everything on Day 1.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;In your role, you&#39;ll...&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Software Engineers (SWEs) and Engineering Managers&lt;/strong&gt; to define project scope, track dependencies, and remove blockers to drive multidisciplinary teams to successful project completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and refine roadmaps&lt;/strong&gt; for your portfolio of operational programs, translating sparse requirements into concrete technical solutions aligned with yearly business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build automation-based workflows&lt;/strong&gt;, workflow agents, and self-service tools within industry-standard engineering systems (such as AWS, Salesforce, Fivetran, Jira, and GitHub) to serve as organizational force multipliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define, collect, and sanitize raw usage data&lt;/strong&gt; to design and implement business intelligence visualizations that inform data-driven decisions and measure program impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Synthesize complex project information&lt;/strong&gt; into accessible narratives, autonomously presenting deliverables tailored for engineering senior leadership and key stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Break down technical solutions&lt;/strong&gt; into meaningful milestones, executing with high confidence and velocity across your program portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operate and deliver projects&lt;/strong&gt; utilizing industry and project management best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt; 2–3 years of experience as a Technical Program Manager (TPM) or in a similar technical program/project management function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt; a background in software development or a deep understanding of software engineering platforms and infrastructure architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt; domain expertise and working Python knowledge in relation to data structures, distributed systems, and business intelligence data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt; proficient in navigating and leveraging tools like Jira, GitHub, AWS, Salesforce, or Fivetran to build modular data preparations and clean visualizations.&lt;/li&gt;
